NOTE ON DATA AND MODEL WEIGHTS

This licence covers the SOURCE CODE only.

The NSCLC-Radiogenomics and NSCLC-Radiomics collections are distributed by The
Cancer Imaging Archive under their own terms (CC BY 3.0 and CC BY-NC 3.0
respectively at time of writing). No imaging or clinical data is included in
this repository. Obtain them from TCIA directly and honour the Data Usage
Policy attached to each collection.

That statement was untrue between 2026-07-20 and 2026-08-12: data/processed_pretrain/
held 421 derived NSCLC-Radiomics .npz files (16 x 224 x 224 windowed CT plus tumour
masks per patient, ~1.0 GB) because .gitignore named data/raw/ and data/processed/
but not the directory added later for the pretraining corpus. The files have been
removed from the working tree and purged from git history, .gitignore now matches
data/ wholesale, and the repository was made private on discovery. Recorded here
rather than quietly corrected, because a licence that misdescribes what it covers
is worse than one that admits it did.

BiomedCLIP and BioGPT carry their own licences from their respective authors.
Trained checkpoints derived from them may inherit those terms.

This software is a research prototype. It is not a medical device, has not been
reviewed or approved by any regulatory body, and must not be used to inform
clinical care.
